		{
			"memberSegmentIndices": [46, 50, 52],
			"route": { "family": "Saying", "kind": "Saying" },
			"notes": {
				"rationale": "Mia's line is Duden's proverb doppelt [genäht] hält besser with gemoppelt for genäht; no collection that de/saying-needs-uptake counts lists the line itself. The bracketed genäht stays in the Canonical Form, as [guten] Morgen gives guten Morgen. The kept words Doppelt, hält and besser are the members, Partial, since genäht is missing (#828). gemoppelt, the replacing word, has a Duden and DWDS headword, so it resolves on its own (de/modification-attests-partially). The line is not the ADJ doppelt gemoppelt: the sense is the proverb's 'doubling is safer', not the ADJ's 'needlessly twice', since Mia packs both copies, and that reading would take the kept Doppelt out of the Saying. The arbitrary unmarked quotation and ordinary assertion remain contextual contrast."
			},
